      "latin": "claudō, claudere, clausī, clausum",
      "status": "alternative",
      "period": "modern",
      "gloss": "shut down (a computer)",
      "evidence": [
        "Traupman 262"
      ]
    },
    {
      "latin": "expediō, expedīre, expedīvī, expedītum",
      "status": "avoid",
      "period": "modern",
      "gloss": "Traupman’s “turn off”",
      "evidence": [
        "Traupman 124: to turn off the light, lūmen expedīre; the radio, radiophōnum expedīre"
      ],
      "comment": "Classically “free, disentangle, get ready” (Lewis &amp; Short); nothing in it suggests switching off. Use <span lang=\"la\">exstinguere</span>."
    }
  ],
  "phrases": [
